    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 131,
        "endIndex": 281,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [15]: Meta, Roblox, and Quora Challenge Ofcom’s Online Safety Act Categorisation**\n* **Publisher:** Financial Times (Daniel Thomas)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 131,
        "endIndex": 494,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [15]: Meta, Roblox, and Quora Challenge Ofcom’s Online Safety Act Categorisation**\n* **Publisher:** Financial Times (Daniel Thomas)\n* **What is confirmed:** Meta has filed a new legal appeal in the UK Upper Tribunal challenging Ofcom’s decision to designate WhatsApp and Instagram as \"Category 1\" services under the UK Online Safety Act (OSA)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 496,
        "endIndex": 684,
        "text": "Meta argues that Category 1 requirements—such as measures against fraudulent advertising and reporting on illegal content—are unsuitable for private and small-group messaging platforms"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 686,
        "endIndex": 782,
        "text": "Roblox and Quora are pursuing separate tribunal appeals against their respective categorisations"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 784,
        "endIndex": 907,
        "text": "This adds to ongoing High Court judicial review proceedings brought by Meta against Ofcom regarding fee and fine structures"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 909,
        "endIndex": 1061,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** UK politicians and policy advocates express concern that tech companies are using litigation to delay implementation of the OSA"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1063,
        "endIndex": 1145,
        "text": "Ofcom has not yet publicly published a full formal response to the tribunal filing"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1278,
        "endIndex": 1437,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [8]: CXMT Begins Mass Production on 5th-Gen DRAM Platform and Unveils 24Gb LPDDR5X Chips**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters / South China Morning Post"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1278,
        "endIndex": 1671,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [8]: CXMT Begins Mass Production on 5th-Gen DRAM Platform and Unveils 24Gb LPDDR5X Chips**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters / South China Morning Post\n* **What is confirmed:** ChangXin Memory Technologies (CXMT), China's top DRAM manufacturer, announced at the 2026 World Manufacturing Convention in Hefei that its fifth-generation (G5) technology platform has entered mass production"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1673,
        "endIndex": 1815,
        "text": "The process reduces memory array feature spacing to 11.95 nanometers using multi-patterning lithography, yielding over 50% more dies per wafer"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1817,
        "endIndex": 1907,
        "text": "CXMT also introduced two 24Gb LPDDR5X mobile memory products manufactured on this new node"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4,
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1909,
        "endIndex": 2055,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** Performance and density claims relative to global market leaders (Samsung, SK Hynix, Micron) represent company assertions"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2057,
        "endIndex": 2145,
        "text": "Due to US export controls on EUV equipment, CXMT relies on multi-exposure DUV techniques"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4,
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2297,
        "endIndex": 2401,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [14]: Trump Announces Plans for New \"AI Czar\" and \"AI Force\"**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        9,
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2297,
        "endIndex": 2584,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [14]: Trump Announces Plans for New \"AI Czar\" and \"AI Force\"**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters\n* **What is confirmed:** US President Donald Trump announced via social media that he intends to create an \"AI Force\" modeled on the Space Force and appoint a new \"AI czar\" / adviser"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        9,
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2586,
        "endIndex": 2765,
        "text": "He reaffirmed a deregulatory stance, stating the administration will not \"hinder or stifle\" AI industry growth and that existing civil/criminal laws are sufficient to handle risks"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        12,
        13
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2767,
        "endIndex": 2883,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The announcement lacks concrete implementation details, timelines, or legislative proposals"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        9,
        13
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2885,
        "endIndex": 3027,
        "text": "Former venture capitalist David Sacks previously filled the AI czar role before stepping down to an external advisory capacity earlier in 2026"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        9,
        13
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3171,
        "endIndex": 3294,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [18]: Nippon Life Plans $13 Billion US Data Center Financing Push**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters / Nikkei Asia"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        14,
        15
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3171,
        "endIndex": 3498,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [18]: Nippon Life Plans $13 Billion US Data Center Financing Push**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters / Nikkei Asia\n* **What is confirmed:** Nippon Life Insurance plans to build a 2 trillion yen (~$12.75 billion) infrastructure project-financing portfolio, primarily targeted at financing US AI data center construction"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        16,
        17
